```javascript
function processDocument(text) {
    const categoryPatterns = {
        'political': [/democracy|dictator|election|revolution|nuclear/gi, {}],
        'military': [/war|siege|bombing|destroyed/gi, {}],
        'scientific': [/(discovery|invention)/gi, {}]
    };

    function extractEvents(text) {
        for (let category in categoryPatterns) {
            let pattern = categoryPatterns[category][0];
            let eventsObj = categoryPatterns[category][1];

            let matches;
            while ((matches = pattern.exec(text)) !== null) {
                let eventName = matches[0].toLowerCase();
                if (eventsObj.hasOwnProperty(eventName))
                    eventsObj[eventName]++;
                else
                    eventsObj[eventName] = 1;
            }
        }
    }

    extractEvents(text);

    let results = {};
    for (let category in categoryPatterns) {
        if (Object.keys(categoryPatterns[category][1]).length > 0)
            results[category] = categoryPatterns[category][1];
    }

    return results;
}
```
This function takes a text document as input, uses regex patterns to identify significant events in the different categories and counts their occurrences. It returns an object with each category represented as a key and its corresponding events/occurrence count as values. If no significant event is found in any of the categories, it returns an empty object. Please note that this function does not handle files exceeding 10 MB as it's not clear how such large documents would be input into this function - if you have a different way of handling very large inputs (like streaming), you may need to adjust this accordingly.
