['Here's an example of what such a function could look like using Java 8 ConcurrentHashMap as cache. Please note that due to limitation of text-based interface, this does not compile without proper class definitions and other required details.

```java
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;
import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;

public class TransactionGroup {
    private static AtomicInteger idCounter = new AtomicInteger(0);
    private Map<String, Integer> parent;
    private Map<String, List<String>> children;

    public TransactionGroup() {
        this.parent = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
        this.children = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    }

    public int getId(String product) {
        parent.putIfAbsent(product, idCounter.incrementAndGet());
        return parent.get(product);
    }

    public void union(int p1, String s2) {
        if (!children.containsKey(s2)) {
            children.put(s2, new ArrayList<>());
        }

        for (String s : children.remove(s2)) {
            parent.put(s, p1);
            children.get(parent.get(s).toString()).add(s);
        }
    }

    public int getGroupCount() {
        return idCounter.get();
    }
}
```

Here's the function:

