    // No reusable block found, allocate new memory from OS
    void* allocatedAddress = malloc(size);

    pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);
    return allocatedAddress;
}
```
This code provides a simple implementation of a custom memory allocator that tries to reuse freed blocks before asking the operating system for new memory. The `free` function would then add the returned address and size back into the free list. Note: This is a very basic example, actual implementation might need to consider many other factors such as alignment, splitting large blocks etc.

For logging, you can use any of your favorite logging libraries or write your own simple logger. For configuration options handling, command line arguments parsing function can be used. 

