['Here's a simple implementation in C. Note that this solution doesn't include the file writing functionality to keep it simple, but you can easily add that yourself. Also note that thread safety has been ensured through use of mutexes (pthread_mutex_lock and pthread_mutex_unlock) for mutual exclusion.

```c
#include <stdarg.h>
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <pthread.h>

// Global variable to track the error count
int errorCount = 0;

// Mutex to protect global variables from concurrent access
pthread_mutex_t mutex = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;

void log_error_condition(int condition, const char *format, ...) {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&mutex);

    if (condition) {
        va_list args;
        ++errorCount;
        va_start(args, format);

        // Check for empty format string to avoid crashing due to snprintf with no arguments.
        if(strlen(format) > 0){
            char buffer[256];
            int result = vsnprintf(buffer, sizeof(buffer), format, args);

            if (result >= 0 && result < sizeof(buffer)) {
                // Write to log file or handle in another appropriate way.
                printf("Log: %s\n", buffer);

                if (errorCount == 10) {
                    printf("Special Warning Message: Error Count has reached 10!\n");
                    errorCount = 0;  // Reset the counter after warning
                }
            } else {
                printf("Error: Buffer size exceeded when formatting message.\n");
            }
        }else{
            printf("Warning: Empty format string received. No message logged.\n");
        }

        va_end(args);
    }

    pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex);
}
``` 
In this example, `condition` is a boolean that determines whether the function should log an error message or not. If it's true, the function formats and logs the error message using the format string and variable arguments. The function also keeps track of how many times the condition has been met and logs a special warning message if this count reaches 10.
