['Sure, here is a basic implementation in C language using `malloc()` for memory allocation and `free()` to release it.

This function generates dynamically allocated arrays with random `CRCFLAG` values and checks for duplicate `RNTI`. If duplicates are found, the array size is increased and reallocation happens again until no duplicates found:

```c
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <time.h>  // For time()
#include <assert.h>

typedef struct NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T {
    int RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG;
    int RNTI;
    int CRC_INDICATION_REL8_TAG;
} NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T;

NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T* allocateAndPopulateArray(int size) {
    srand((unsigned int)time(NULL)); // initialize random seed
    NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T *array = malloc(sizeof(*array) * size);
    assert(array != NULL && "Memory allocation failed");

    while (1) {
        int duplicateFound = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < size; ++i) {
            array[i].RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG = rand(); // randomly set values
            array[i].RNTI = rand(); 
            array[i].CRC_INDICATION_REL8_TAG = rand() % 2; // 0 or 1 for CRCFLAG
        }

        // Check duplicates
        for (int i = 0; i < size - 1 && !duplicateFound; ++i) {
            for (int j = i + 1; j < size && !duplicateFound; ++j) {
                if (array[i].RNTI == array[j].RNTI) {
                    duplicateFound = 1;
                }
            }
        }

        // If duplicates found, increase the array size and try again.
        if (duplicateFound) {
            ++size;
            NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T *tmp = realloc(array, sizeof(*array) * size);
            assert((tmp != NULL || size == 1) && "Memory allocation failed");
            // If the new block is allocated successfully and it's not the first run of the loop.
            if (tmp != NULL) {
                array = tmp;
            }
        } else {
            break;
        }
    }

    return array;
}
```

The function `allocateAndPopulateArray` allocates an array of `NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T` structures and populates them with randomly generated values. It checks for duplicate `RNTI` values, if found then it increments the size of the array by one and tries again to populate it until no duplicates are found.

In case of a memory allocation failure (`malloc` or `realloc` returns NULL), an error message will be printed on stderr and the program will terminate with an abort signal. 

The function has not been tested, but should work as described provided that a C99 compiler is used. Please adjust it according to your project requirements.
